add('### Models, training and all results')
add('Inputs are mean, sample SD and CV over trailing 7/14/30 observed entries, trailing-30 zero-income fraction, and latest income divided by trailing-30 mean (11 features). They include today\'s income because this is current-state classification. All means/scales are estimated from training only; later test features may use past observed validation/test incomes but no past/future label values as predictors. An automated poisoning test confirms that changing the future test suffix cannot affect training/validation features or scores, and changing either label or stored rolling column cannot affect features.')
add('Comparators: training-majority label; unchanged runtime classifier; window-7/14/30 quantile CV rules fitted to training-only order statistics; ordered low/medium/high CV threshold classifiers, optimizing training original-label macro-F1 over midpoints between adjacent distinct training CVs; standardized Gaussian naive Bayes with empirical class priors and variance smoothing 1e-6/.01/.1; standardized nearest centroids with uniform or inverse-frequency prediction priors; standardized Euclidean kNN with k=5/15/31 and stable row-order/class-order ties. Standardized features use training population SD with a 1e-9 floor. NB adds the stated smoothing constant to per-class standardized population variance. This is an explicit dependency-free implementation, not a claim of scikit-learn equivalence.')
add(f'One global candidate is selected by validation original-label macro-F1, then balanced accuracy and declared order: `{vc}`. It is refit on training+validation before test predictions. Every fixed candidate is scored on the same test set for transparency; the selected method is not switched to a test winner. Macro-F1 averages per-class F1 over low/medium/high; balanced accuracy is mean per-class recall. Unsupported predictions have precision/F1 zero. All original-target classes are represented in every partition.')
