add('## 6. Automated tests, failed experiments and remaining limitations')
add('The new Node suite uses the built-in node:test/strict assert framework; the Python suite uses unittest. Tests cover policy combinations, threshold equality and sub-rupee violations, missing/malformed inputs, error/unknown analytics, complete-request omission, stale/forged cached flags, the controller read path, valid users still receiving recommendations, actual Python-to-Node payload compatibility, deterministic statistical baselines, sample metric calculation, causal feature construction, train-only scaling, frozen selection-file hashes and disjoint validation/test targets. No test dependency was installed.')
table(['Suite','Tests','Passed','Failed','Errors','Exit code'],[[name,r['total'],r['passed'],r['failed'],r['errors'],r.get('exit_code','aggregate')] for name,r in tests.items()])
add('The new suites pass. The retained Python regression/requirement suite still fails `test_zero_income_is_not_low_risk`: the unchanged classifier treats an all-zero income history as CV=0 / low. This was not hidden or changed to make a green suite. The revised router independently rejects zero mean/zero-only forecast inputs. The combined test runner reports the retained failure and intentionally exits with code 1 whenever any suite has a failure. The captured pre-change broader audit had '+str(base['tests']['passed']+bn['test_summary']['passed'])+' passes and '+str(base['tests']['failed']+bn['test_summary']['failed'])+' failures across '+str(base['tests']['total']+bn['test_summary']['total'])+' named tests. Its old Node fixtures/oracles do not match the new mandatory schema/policy, so they were preserved as historical evidence rather than misleadingly counted as directly comparable post-fix tests.')
add('Failed or incomplete experiments and scope limits:')
add('- Forecast deployment gate failed because selected validation RMSE worsened versus historical mean. Test improvement is reported without changing that decision. Several statistical candidates perform poorly; all fixed candidates remain in the tables. Full packaged ARIMA/ETS fitting was not attempted after confirming missing scientific dependencies, because explicit small alternatives already cover the requested lightweight comparison.\n- Volatility high-class recall worsened despite macro-F1 improvement. Provided labels remain synthetic and not independently annotated, and adjacent rolling windows overlap. No supervised model replaced runtime labels.\n- Threshold/weight policy conformance is not prospective financial safety, health-score validation, investment suitability or financial-outcome validation. No real-worker generalization, independent cohort, profitability, return backtest, fairness or usability result is established.\n- No novel forecasting or classification algorithm is claimed. Hyperparameter exploration is limited but does not eliminate overfitting on a small retrospective synthetic corpus. No statistical significance or uncertainty interval is asserted.\n- The router does not verify provenance or age of analytics, rederive labels from raw income, reconcile all cached dashboard/explanation views, or make concurrent reads transactional. Valid-looking erroneous summaries can still pass policy checks; future work needs input/version binding and independently validated risk signals.\n- LLM validation/fallback problems, health-score income invariance/expense-normalization behavior, and product allocation feasibility from the earlier audit are outside these three targeted fixes. No new live LLM, market-performance or database-integration experiment was run.\n- Code coverage percentage was not remeasured for this change. Earlier Python-only line-trace numbers must not be presented as current full-system coverage. New tests run with in-memory DB adapters, not a deployed MongoDB instance or full browser session.')
add('A remaining allocation-minimum defect was explicitly re-executed after the safety patch, rather than inferred solely from the old audit. A safe-policy profile with '+str(defects['profile'])+f' receives health={defects["health"]}, eligible={defects["eligible"]}, investable={defects["investable"]}. Final allocations remain below the stored product minima:')
table(['Product ID','Allocated Rs','Stored minimum Rs'],[[x['id'],x['amount'],x['minimum']] for x in defects['allocations']])
add('Thus “zero policy false allows” must not be expanded into a claim that all returned product allocations are executable or that every recommended action is practically safe. The smallest next engineering fix is minimum-aware allocation or returning fewer feasible products; that was not conflated with the router metrics or silently patched as a fourth target.')

